.Dd October 9, 2026
.Dt TRY-PATHS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm try-paths
.Nd list, add, and remove try-rs source folders
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm list
.Nm
.Cm add
.Op Ar dir
.Op Fl -at Ar N | Fl -first
.Nm
.Cm rm
.Op Ar dir | number
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
changes the
.Va tries_path
setting of try-rs.
Each folder in
.Va tries_path
is one tab in the try-rs TUI.
Use the left and right arrow keys to move between the tabs.
The first folder is the folder where
.Ql try <name>
creates a new try.
.Pp
.Nm
rewrites only the
.Va tries_path
line.
The comments and the other settings in the file do not change.
If the config file is a symlink,
.Nm
writes to the target of the symlink and keeps the symlink.
Paths under
.Ev HOME
are stored in the
.Pa ~/...
form.
.Pp
After each change,
.Nm
prints the new list of tabs.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm list , Cm ls
Print each tab with its number.
This is the default command.
.It Cm add Oo Ar dir Oc Op Fl -at Ar N | Fl -first
Add
.Ar dir
as the last tab.
If there is no
.Ar dir ,
add the current folder.
.Ar dir
can be absolute, relative, or start with
.Pa ~ .
The folder must exist and must not already be a tab.
.It Cm rm , Cm remove Op Ar dir | number
Remove a tab by its path or by its number from
.Cm list .
If there is no argument, remove the current folder.
.Nm
does not remove the last tab.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -at Ar N , Fl -at= Ns Ar N
Insert the folder as tab
.Ar N .
Tab
.Ar N
and each tab after it move back by one.
.Ar N
must be from 1 to the number of tabs plus 1.
.It Fl -first
The same as
.Fl -at Ar 1 .
The new folder becomes the folder where
.Ql try <name>
creates a new try.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the help text.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev TRY_CONFIG_DIR
The folder that contains the config file.
The default is
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/try-rs .
.It Ev TRY_CONFIG
The name of the config file.
The default is
.Pa config.toml .
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The default is
.Pa ~/.config .
.El
.Pp
.Ev TRY_PATH
overrides
.Va tries_path
in try-rs, but
.Nm
ignores it.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/try-rs/config.toml
The try-rs config file.
In the dotfiles, this is a symlink to
.Pa xdg_config/try-rs/config.toml .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Nm
exits with 1 if the config file is missing, if a folder does not exist,
if a folder is already a tab or is not a tab, if a number is out of range,
or if the arguments are not correct.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Add the current folder as the last tab:
.Dl $ cd ~/projects/activitywatch && try-paths add
.Pp
Add a folder as tab 3:
.Dl $ try-paths add ~/projects/activitywatch --at 3
.Pp
Make a folder the folder where new tries go:
.Dl $ try-paths add ~/projects/tries --first
.Pp
Remove tab 4:
.Dl $ try-paths rm 4
.Pp
Remove the current folder:
.Dl $ try-paths rm
.Sh SEE ALSO
try-rs:
.Lk https://github.com/tassiovirginio/try-rs
